# Excluded from `func azure functionapp publish`'s upload (`func start` does not read this file).
#
# Patterns use .gitignore syntax, so an unanchored name matches at ANY depth: a bare `src` would also strip
# `node_modules/tesseract.js/src/`, which is tesseract.js's entry point, and the deployed Function would die on
# its first image. Everything below is anchored to this folder with a leading `/` for that reason.
#
# `src/` and the tsconfig files are deliberately NOT excluded: a remote build (the default for Flex Consumption,
# and the only way sharp gets linux-x64 binaries) runs `npm run build` on the server, which needs them.

/test
/scripts
/local.settings.json
/local.settings.json.example
/.env
/.env.*
/.git*
/.funcignore
/README.md

# @tesseract.js-data/eng ships more than one accuracy variant of the model (10 MB vs. 2.8 MB); only
# 4.0.0_best_int is loaded (src/core/env.ts resolveLangPath), so the plain 4.0.0 one is dead weight to deploy.
/node_modules/@tesseract.js-data/eng/4.0.0/
